# Blueprint harness renames
#
# Applied by `blueprint update` (and install/sync projections) before writing
# managed skills/rules into consumer runtimes (.cursor / .claude).
#
# Purpose: when a package skill or rule is renamed, remove the old path from
# target projects so rebuilds do not leave stale folders beside the new name.
#
# Format (whitespace-separated; # comments and blank lines ignored):
#   kind    old_name                              new_name
#
# kind:
#   skill   → directory under <runtime>/skills/<name>/
#   rule    → file under <runtime>/rules/<name>
#             (.mdc listed; Claude projections also remove the .md twin)
#
# Append a row whenever you rename a managed skill or rule. Do not delete
# historical rows — update replays the full log for every target.

skill  memory-system-protocol           context-recall
skill  planning-execution-tracking      task-execution
rule   planning-execution-tracking.mdc  task-execution.mdc
skill  testcase-generator               generate-test-cases
